# Draft-prompt smoke runs. These exist to prove the scripts execute, nothing
# more. TASK.md is not final, so these runs describe a prompt that will not be
# the published one — they are not evidence, and they never count toward the
# hit rate the README promises to publish. Kept out of the repo so they cannot
# be mistaken for the archive.
transcripts/smoke/
# transcripts/archive/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the archive is the
# published record, and a hit rate over runs nobody else can read is an
# assertion rather than evidence.

# verify.sh snapshots written by the run scripts into this directory. Same
# reasoning: products of draft-prompt runs.
before.txt
after.txt
before-taper.txt
after-taper.txt
